==== status
h2: High Availability Status
Real-time status of the HA cluster. Updates every 5 seconds.
h3: Cluster Status
| Cluster Overview
| Cluster State | DEGRADED
| Node Role | MASTER
| Instance: 1 | MASTER
| Instance: 2 | MASTER
| Last Synchronization
| Config Sync | <time>
| Lease Sync | <time>
h3: Service Status
| Service | Status | PID | Uptime
| keepalived | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| owsync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
| lease-sync | Running | <pid> | <uptime>
h3: Peer Status
| Peer Name | Address | State | Last Seen
| vrrp-box | 192.168.50.30 | Offline | Unreachable
==== simple
h2: High Availability - General
Configure a high availability cluster with 2 or more routers. Advanced options are available in the Advanced pages.
h3: Cluster Configuration
config.enabled [CBI.FlagValue] Enable HA Cluster: [x]
  help: Enable high availability clustering on this router
config.node_priority [CBI.Value] Priority: value=100 (placeholder "100")
  help: VRRP priority (1-255). Higher priority becomes MASTER.
config.vrrp_transport [CBI.ListValue] VRRP Transport: select=multicast {multicast,unicast}
  help: Multicast is the default. Use unicast when multicast is unavailable on the network.
h3: Peer Routers
| Peer | 
| <anon>: vrrp-box (192.168.50.30) | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add
h3: Virtual IP Addresses
All VIPs share a single failover group and switch together. Use the Advanced page to create independent failover groups. Optional. If IPv6 is configured, keepalived creates a second instance with VRID+128.
| Interface | VRID | IPv4 Address | IPv6 Address | Enable | 
| <anon>: <img> lan | 64 | 192.168.50.254 | none | Yes | [☰][Edit][Delete]
<button> Add VIP...
h3: Configuration Synchronization
Select which /etc/config files to synchronize and how synchronization is performed.
config.encryption_key [CBI.Value] Encryption Key: password= (placeholder "Click "Generate New Key" button below to create a secure random key") button "∗"
  help: 256-bit AES encryption key (64 hexadecimal characters) for configuration sync (owsync) and DHCP lease sync (lease-sync). Must be identical on all cluster nodes. Leave empty to disable encryption.
config._generate_key [CBI.ButtonValue] Generate New Key: button "Generate New Key"
config._dhcp_leases [CBI.FlagValue] Enable Real-time DHCP Lease Sync: [ ]
  help: Synchronize DHCP leases in real-time using the lease-sync daemon for seamless client failover
config.sync_method [CBI.ListValue] Sync Method: select=none {owsync,none}
  help: owsync: real-time file synchronization. none: disable file synchronization.
config._dhcp_config [CBI.FlagValue] Sync DHCP Configuration: [ ]
  help: Synchronize /etc/config/dhcp (address pools, static leases, DNS settings)
config._firewall_config [CBI.FlagValue] Sync Firewall Rules: [ ]
  help: Synchronize /etc/config/firewall (port forwarding, rules, zones). Review rules before enabling.
